# AI economy bias (user design, 2026-07-17): virtual, amortized per-minute
# consumption of the NON-CONSTANT costs — building construction, unit
# recruitment, tower ammunition — added to the consumption telemetry the AI
# senses (never to the real telemetry the HUD shows). The AI works to keep
# production >= consumption, so this bias forces it to stand up and SUSTAIN
# production of these resources instead of stalling once its starting stock
# runs dry (playtest 2026-07-17: roads stopped dead when STONE ran out).
#
# Values are hand-tuned per-minute averages. difficulty_scale multiplies
# them per AI difficulty level (0 Primitive .. 3 Hard) — a better-tuned,
# fuller bias equals a stronger economy, i.e. a harder opponent.
ai_economy_bias
    difficulty_scale 0.4 0.6 0.8 1.0
    consumption WOOD 12
    consumption STONE 10
    consumption PLANKS 8
    consumption IRON 4
    consumption TOOLS 2
    consumption FOOD_PROVISIONS 10
    consumption ARROWS 6
end
